bible_data_cache["bsb_Mark"] = [
[
"001:001 This is the beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, the Son of God.",
"001:002 As it is written in Isaiah the prophet: “Behold, I will send My messenger ahead of You, who will prepare Your way.”",
"001:003 “A voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way for the Lord, make straight paths for Him.’”",
"001:004 John the Baptist appeared in the wilderness, preaching a baptism of repentance for the forgiveness of sins.",
"001:005 People went out to him from all of Jerusalem and the countryside of Judea. Confessing their sins, they were baptized by him in the Jordan River.",
"001:006 John was clothed in camel’s hair, with a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.",
"001:007 And he proclaimed: “After me will come One more powerful than I, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to stoop down and untie.",
"001:008 I baptize you with water, but He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit.”",
"001:009 In those days Jesus came from Nazareth in Galilee and was baptized by John in the Jordan.",
"001:010 As soon as Jesus came up out of the water, He saw the heavens breaking open and the Spirit descending on Him like a dove.",
"001:011 And a voice came from heaven: “You are My beloved Son; in You I am well pleased.”",
"001:012 At once the Spirit drove Jesus into the wilderness,",
"001:013 and He was there for forty days, being tempted by Satan. He was with the wild animals, and the angels ministered to Him.",
"001:014 After the arrest of John, Jesus went into Galilee and proclaimed the gospel of God.",
"001:015 “The time is fulfilled,” He said, “and the kingdom of God is near. Repent and believe in the gospel!”",
"001:016 As Jesus was walking beside the Sea of Galilee, He saw Simon and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the sea, for they were fishermen.",
"001:017 “Come, follow Me,” Jesus said, “and I will make you fishers of men.”",
"001:018 And at once they left their nets and followed Him.",
"001:019 Going on a little farther, He saw James son of Zebedee and his brother John. They were in a boat, mending their nets.",
"001:020 Immediately Jesus called them, and they left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired men and followed Him.",
"001:021 Then Jesus and His companions went to Capernaum, and right away Jesus entered the synagogue on the Sabbath and began to teach.",
"001:022 The people were astonished at His teaching, because He taught as one who had authority, and not as the scribes.",
"001:023 Suddenly a man with an unclean spirit cried out in the synagogue:",
"001:024 “What do You want with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have You come to destroy us? I know who You are—the Holy One of God!”",
"001:025 But Jesus rebuked the spirit. “Be silent!” He said. “Come out of him!”",
"001:026 At this, the unclean spirit threw the man into convulsions and came out with a loud shriek.",
"001:027 All the people were amazed and began to ask one another, “What is this? A new teaching with authority! He commands even the unclean spirits, and they obey Him!”",
"001:028 And the news about Jesus spread quickly through the whole region of Galilee.",
"001:029 As soon as Jesus and His companions had left the synagogue, they went with James and John to the home of Simon and Andrew.",
"001:030 Simon’s mother-in-law was sick in bed with a fever, and they promptly told Jesus about her.",
"001:031 So He went to her, took her by the hand, and helped her up. The fever left her, and she began to serve them.",
"001:032 That evening, after sunset, people brought to Jesus all the sick and demon-possessed,",
"001:033 and the whole town gathered at the door.",
"001:034 And He healed many who were ill with various diseases and drove out many demons. But He would not allow the demons to speak, because they knew who He was.",
"001:035 Early in the morning, while it was still dark, Jesus got up and went out to a solitary place to pray.",
"001:036 Simon and his companions went to look for Him,",
"001:037 and when they found Him, they said, “Everyone is looking for You!”",
"001:038 But Jesus answered, “Let us go on to the neighboring towns so I can preach there as well, for that is why I have come.”",
"001:039 So He went throughout Galilee, preaching in their synagogues and driving out demons.",
"001:040 Then a leper came to Jesus, begging on his knees: “If You are willing, You can make me clean.”",
"001:041 Moved with compassion, Jesus reached out His hand and touched the man. “I am willing,” He said. “Be clean!”",
"001:042 And immediately the leprosy left him, and the man was cleansed.",
"001:043 Jesus promptly sent him away with a stern warning:",
"001:044 “See that you don’t tell anyone. But go, show yourself to the priest and present the offering Moses prescribed for your cleansing, as a testimony to them.”",
"001:045 But the man went out and openly began to proclaim and spread the news. Consequently, Jesus could no longer enter a town in plain view, but He stayed out in solitary places. Yet people came to Him from every quarter."
],
[
"002:001 A few days later Jesus went back to Capernaum. And when the people heard that He was home,",
"002:002 they gathered in such large numbers that there was no more room, not even outside the door, as Jesus spoke the word to them.",
"002:003 Then a paralytic was brought to Him, carried by four men.",
"002:004 Since they were unable to get to Jesus through the crowd, they uncovered the roof above Him, made an opening, and lowered the paralytic on his mat.",
"002:005 When Jesus saw their faith, He said to the paralytic, “Son, your sins are forgiven.”",
"002:006 But some of the scribes were sitting there and thinking in their hearts,",
"002:007 “Why does this man speak like this? He is blaspheming! Who can forgive sins but God alone?”",
"002:008 At once Jesus knew in His spirit that they were thinking this way within themselves. “Why are you thinking these things in your hearts?” He asked.",
"002:009 “Which is easier: to say to a paralytic, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Get up, pick up your mat, and walk’?",
"002:010 But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins...” He said to the paralytic,",
"002:011 “I tell you, get up, pick up your mat, and go home.”",
"002:012 And immediately the man got up, picked up his mat, and walked out in front of them all. As a result, they were all astounded and glorified God, saying, “We have never seen anything like this!”",
"002:013 Once again Jesus went out beside the sea. All the people came to Him, and He taught them there.",
"002:014 As He was walking along, He saw Levi son of Alphaeus sitting at the tax booth. “Follow Me,” He told him, and Levi got up and followed Him.",
"002:015 While Jesus was dining at Levi’s house, many tax collectors and sinners were eating with Him and His disciples—for there were many who followed Him.",
"002:016 When the scribes who were Pharisees saw Jesus eating with these people, they asked His disciples, “Why does He eat with tax collectors and sinners?”",
"002:017 On hearing this, Jesus told them, “It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick. I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners.”",
"002:018 Now John’s disciples and the Pharisees were often fasting. So people came to Jesus and asked, “Why don’t Your disciples fast like John’s disciples and those of the Pharisees?”",
"002:019 Jesus replied, “How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while He is with them? As long as He is with them, they cannot fast.",
"002:020 But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them; then they will fast.",
"002:021 No one sews a patch of unshrunk cloth on an old garment. If he does, the new piece will pull away from the old, and a worse tear will result.",
"002:022 And no one pours new wine into old wineskins. If he does, the wine will burst the skins, and both the wine and the wineskins will be ruined. Instead, new wine is poured into new wineskins.”",
"002:023 One Sabbath Jesus was passing through the grainfields, and His disciples began to pick the heads of grain as they walked along.",
"002:024 So the Pharisees said to Him, “Look, why are they doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath?”",
"002:025 Jesus replied, “Have you never read what David did when he and his companions were hungry and in need?",
"002:026 During the high priesthood of Abiathar, he entered the house of God and ate the consecrated bread, which was lawful only for the priests. And he gave some to his companions as well.”",
"002:027 Then Jesus declared, “The Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath.",
"002:028 Therefore, the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath.”"
],
[
"003:001 Once again Jesus entered the synagogue, and a man with a withered hand was there.",
"003:002 In order to accuse Jesus, they were watching to see if He would heal on the Sabbath.",
"003:003 Then Jesus said to the man with the withered hand, “Stand up among us.”",
"003:004 And He asked them, “Which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to destroy it?” But they were silent.",
"003:005 Jesus looked around at them with anger and sorrow at their hardness of heart. Then He said to the man, “Stretch out your hand.” So he stretched it out, and it was restored.",
"003:006 At this, the Pharisees went out and began plotting with the Herodians how they might kill Jesus.",
"003:007 So Jesus withdrew with His disciples to the sea, accompanied by a large crowd from Galilee, Judea,",
"003:008 Jerusalem, Idumea, the region beyond the Jordan, and the vicinity of Tyre and Sidon. The large crowd came to Him when they heard what great things He was doing.",
"003:009 Jesus asked His disciples to have a boat ready for Him so that the crowd would not crush Him.",
"003:010 For He had healed so many that all who had diseases were pressing forward to touch Him.",
"003:011 And when the unclean spirits saw Him, they fell down before Him and cried out, “You are the Son of God!”",
"003:012 But He warned them sternly not to make Him known.",
"003:013 Then Jesus went up on the mountain and called for those He wanted, and they came to Him.",
"003:014 He appointed twelve of them, whom He designated as apostles, to accompany Him, to be sent out to preach,",
"003:015 and to have authority to drive out demons.",
"003:016 These are the twelve He appointed: Simon (whom He named Peter),",
"003:017 James son of Zebedee and his brother John (whom He named Boanerges, meaning “Sons of Thunder”),",
"003:018 Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, James son of Alphaeus, Thaddaeus, Simon the Zealot,",
"003:019 and Judas Iscariot, who betrayed Jesus.",
"003:020 Then Jesus went home, and once again a crowd gathered, so that He and His disciples could not even eat.",
"003:021 When His family heard about this, they went out to take custody of Him, saying, “He is out of His mind.”",
"003:022 And the scribes who had come down from Jerusalem were saying, “He is possessed by Beelzebul,” and, “By the prince of the demons He drives out demons.”",
"003:023 So Jesus called them together and began to speak to them in parables: “How can Satan drive out Satan?",
"003:024 If a kingdom is divided against itself, it cannot stand.",
"003:025 If a house is divided against itself, it cannot stand.",
"003:026 And if Satan is divided and rises against himself, he cannot stand; his end has come.",
"003:027 Indeed, no one can enter a strong man’s house to steal his possessions unless he first ties up the strong man. Then he can plunder his house.",
"003:028 Truly I tell you, the sons of men will be forgiven all sins and blasphemies, as many as they utter.",
"003:029 But whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will never be forgiven; he is guilty of eternal sin.”",
"003:030 Jesus made this statement because they were saying, “He has an unclean spirit.”",
"003:031 Then Jesus’ mother and brothers came and stood outside. They sent someone in to summon Him,",
"003:032 and a crowd was sitting around Him. “Look,” He was told, “Your mother and brothers are outside, asking for You.”",
"003:033 But Jesus replied, “Who are My mother and My brothers?”",
"003:034 Looking at those seated in a circle around Him, He said, “Here are My mother and My brothers!",
"003:035 For whoever does the will of God is My brother and sister and mother.”"
],
[
"004:001 Once again Jesus began to teach beside the sea, and such a large crowd gathered around Him that He got into a boat and sat in it, while all the people crowded along the shore.",
"004:002 And He taught them many things in parables, and in His teaching He said,",
"004:003 “Listen! A farmer went out to sow his seed.",
"004:004 And as he was sowing, some seed fell along the path, and the birds came and devoured it.",
"004:005 Some fell on rocky ground, where it did not have much soil. It sprang up quickly because the soil was shallow.",
"004:006 But when the sun rose, the seedlings were scorched, and they withered because they had no root.",
"004:007 Other seed fell among thorns, which grew up and choked the seedlings, and they yielded no crop.",
"004:008 Still other seed fell on good soil, where it sprouted, grew up, and produced a crop—one bearing thirtyfold, another sixtyfold, and another a hundredfold.”",
"004:009 Then Jesus said, “He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”",
"004:010 As soon as Jesus was alone with the Twelve and those around Him, they asked Him about the parable.",
"004:011 He replied, “The mystery of the kingdom of God has been given to you, but to those on the outside everything is expressed in parables,",
"004:012 so that, ‘they may be ever seeing but never perceiving, and ever hearing but never understanding; otherwise they might turn and be forgiven.’”",
"004:013 Then Jesus said to them, “Do you not understand this parable? Then how will you understand any of the parables?",
"004:014 The farmer sows the word.",
"004:015 Some are like the seeds along the path, where the word is sown. As soon as they hear it, Satan comes and takes away the word that was sown in them.",
"004:016 Some are like the seeds sown on rocky ground. They hear the word and at once receive it with joy.",
"004:017 But they themselves have no root, and they remain for only a season. When trouble or persecution comes because of the word, they quickly fall away.",
"004:018 Others are like the seeds sown among the thorns. They hear the word,",
"004:019 but the worries of this life, the deceitfulness of wealth, and the desire for other things come in and choke the word, and it becomes unfruitful.",
"004:020 Still others are like the seeds sown on good soil. They hear the word, receive it, and produce a crop—thirtyfold, sixtyfold, or a hundredfold.”",
"004:021 Jesus also said to them, “Does anyone bring in a lamp to put it under a basket or under a bed? Doesn’t he set it on a stand?",
"004:022 For there is nothing hidden that will not be disclosed, and nothing concealed that will not be brought to light.",
"004:023 If anyone has ears to hear, let him hear.”",
"004:024 He went on to say, “Pay attention to what you hear. With the measure you use, it will be measured to you, and even more will be added to you.",
"004:025 For whoever has will be given more. But whoever does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.”",
"004:026 Jesus also said, “The kingdom of God is like a man who scatters seed on the ground.",
"004:027 Night and day he sleeps and wakes, and the seed sprouts and grows, though he knows not how.",
"004:028 All by itself the earth produces a crop—first the stalk, then the head, then grain that ripens within.",
"004:029 And as soon as the grain is ripe, he swings the sickle, because the harvest has come.”",
"004:030 Then He asked, “To what can we compare the kingdom of God? With what parable shall we present it?",
"004:031 It is like a mustard seed, which is the smallest of all seeds sown upon the earth.",
"004:032 But after it is planted, it grows to be the largest of all garden plants and puts forth great branches, so that the birds of the air nest in its shade.”",
"004:033 With many such parables Jesus spoke the word to them, to the extent that they could understand.",
"004:034 He did not tell them anything without using a parable. But privately He explained everything to His own disciples.",
"004:035 When that evening came, He said to His disciples, “Let us cross to the other side.”",
"004:036 After they had dismissed the crowd, they took Jesus with them, since He was already in the boat. And there were other boats with Him.",
"004:037 Soon a violent windstorm came up, and the waves were breaking over the boat, so that it was being swamped.",
"004:038 But Jesus was in the stern, sleeping on the cushion. So they woke Him and said, “Teacher, don’t You care that we are perishing?”",
"004:039 Then Jesus got up and rebuked the wind and the sea. “Silence!” He commanded. “Be still!” And the wind died down, and it was perfectly calm.",
"004:040 “Why are you so afraid?” He asked. “Do you still have no faith?”",
"004:041 Overwhelmed with fear, they asked one another, “Who is this, that even the wind and the sea obey Him?”"
],
[
"005:001 On the other side of the sea, they arrived in the region of the Gerasenes.",
"005:002 As soon as Jesus got out of the boat, He was met by a man with an unclean spirit, who was coming from the tombs.",
"005:003 This man had been living in the tombs and could no longer be restrained, even with chains.",
"005:004 Though he was often bound with chains and shackles, he had broken the chains and shattered the shackles. Now there was no one with the strength to subdue him.",
"005:005 Night and day in the tombs and in the mountains he kept crying out and cutting himself with stones.",
"005:006 When the man saw Jesus from a distance, he ran and fell on his knees before Him.",
"005:007 And he shouted in a loud voice, “What do You want with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I beg You before God not to torture me!”",
"005:008 For Jesus had already declared, “Come out of this man, you unclean spirit!”",
"005:009 “What is your name?” Jesus asked. “My name is Legion,” he replied, “for we are many.”",
"005:010 And he begged Jesus repeatedly not to send them out of that region.",
"005:011 There on the nearby hillside a large herd of pigs was feeding.",
"005:012 So the demons begged Jesus, “Send us to the pigs, so that we may enter them.”",
"005:013 He gave them permission, and the unclean spirits came out and went into the pigs, and the herd of about two thousand rushed down the steep bank into the sea and drowned in the water.",
"005:014 Those tending the pigs ran off and reported this in the town and countryside, and the people went out to see what had happened.",
"005:015 When they came to Jesus, they saw the man who had been possessed by the legion of demons sitting there, clothed and in his right mind; and they were afraid.",
"005:016 Those who had seen it described what had happened to the demon-possessed man and also to the pigs.",
"005:017 And the people began to beg Jesus to leave their region.",
"005:018 As He was getting into the boat, the man who had been possessed by the demons begged to go with Him.",
"005:019 But Jesus would not allow him. “Go home to your own people,” He said, “and tell them how much the Lord has done for you, and what mercy He has shown you.”",
"005:020 So the man went away and began to proclaim throughout the Decapolis how much Jesus had done for him. And everyone was amazed.",
"005:021 When Jesus had again crossed by boat to the other side, a large crowd gathered around Him beside the sea.",
"005:022 A synagogue leader named Jairus arrived, and seeing Jesus, he fell at His feet",
"005:023 and pleaded with Him urgently, “My little daughter is near death. Please come and place Your hands on her, so that she will be healed and live.”",
"005:024 So Jesus went with him, and a large crowd followed and pressed around Him.",
"005:025 And a woman was there who had suffered from bleeding for twelve years.",
"005:026 She had borne much agony under the care of many physicians and had spent all she had, but to no avail. Instead, her condition had only grown worse.",
"005:027 When the woman heard about Jesus, she came up through the crowd behind Him and touched His cloak.",
"005:028 For she kept saying, “If only I touch His garments, I will be healed.”",
"005:029 Immediately her bleeding stopped, and she sensed in her body that she was healed of her affliction.",
"005:030 At once Jesus was aware that power had gone out from Him. Turning to the crowd, He asked, “Who touched My garments?”",
"005:031 His disciples answered, “You can see the crowd pressing in on You, and yet You ask, ‘Who touched Me?’”",
"005:032 But He kept looking around to see who had done this.",
"005:033 Then the woman, knowing what had happened to her, came and fell down before Him trembling in fear, and she told Him the whole truth.",
"005:034 “Daughter,” said Jesus, “your faith has healed you. Go in peace and be free of your affliction.”",
"005:035 While He was still speaking, messengers from the house of Jairus arrived and said, “Your daughter is dead; why bother the Teacher anymore?”",
"005:036 But Jesus overheard their conversation and said to Jairus, “Do not be afraid; just believe.”",
"005:037 And He did not allow anyone to accompany Him except Peter, James, and John the brother of James.",
"005:038 When they arrived at the house of the synagogue leader, Jesus saw the commotion and the people weeping and wailing loudly.",
"005:039 He went inside and asked, “Why all this commotion and weeping? The child is not dead, but asleep.”",
"005:040 And they laughed at Him. After He had put them all outside, He took the child’s father and mother and His own companions, and went in to see the child.",
"005:041 Taking her by the hand, Jesus said, “Talitha koum!” which means, “Little girl, I say to you, get up!”",
"005:042 Immediately the girl got up and began to walk around (she was twelve years old). And at once they were utterly astounded.",
"005:043 Then Jesus gave strict orders that no one should know about this, and He told them to give her something to eat."
],
[
"006:001 Jesus went on from there and came to His hometown, accompanied by His disciples.",
"006:002 When the Sabbath came, He began to teach in the synagogue, and many who heard Him were astonished. “Where did this man get these ideas?” they asked. “What is this wisdom He has been given? And how can He perform such miracles?",
"006:003 Isn’t this the carpenter, the son of Mary and the brother of James, Joses, Judas, and Simon? Aren’t His sisters here with us as well?” And they took offense at Him.",
"006:004 Then Jesus said to them, “Only in his hometown, among his relatives, and in his own household is a prophet without honor.”",
"006:005 So He could not perform any miracles there, except to lay His hands on a few of the sick and heal them.",
"006:006 And He was amazed at their unbelief. And He went around from village to village, teaching the people.",
"006:007 Then Jesus called the Twelve to Him and began to send them out two by two, giving them authority over unclean spirits.",
"006:008 He instructed them to take nothing but a staff for the journey—no bread, no bag, no money in their belts—",
"006:009 and to wear sandals, but not a second tunic.",
"006:010 And He told them, “When you enter a house, stay there until you leave that area.",
"006:011 If anyone will not welcome you or listen to you, shake the dust off your feet when you leave that place, as a testimony against them.”",
"006:012 So they set out and preached that the people should repent.",
"006:013 They also drove out many demons and healed many of the sick, anointing them with oil.",
"006:014 Now King Herod heard about this, for Jesus’ name had become well known, and people were saying, “John the Baptist has risen from the dead! That is why miraculous powers are at work in him.”",
"006:015 Others were saying, “He is Elijah,” and still others, “He is a prophet, like one of the prophets of old.”",
"006:016 But when Herod heard this, he said, “John, whom I beheaded, has risen from the dead!”",
"006:017 For Herod himself had ordered that John be arrested and bound and imprisoned, on account of his brother Philip’s wife Herodias, whom Herod had married.",
"006:018 For John had been telling Herod, “It is not lawful for you to have your brother’s wife!”",
"006:019 So Herodias held a grudge against John and wanted to kill him. But she had been unable,",
"006:020 because Herod feared John and protected him, knowing that he was a righteous and holy man. When he heard John’s words, he was greatly perplexed; yet he listened to him gladly.",
"006:021 On Herod’s birthday, her opportunity arose. Herod held a banquet for his nobles and military commanders and the leading men of Galilee.",
"006:022 When the daughter of Herodias came and danced, she pleased Herod and his guests, and the king said to the girl, “Ask me for whatever you wish, and I will give it to you.”",
"006:023 And he swore to her, “Whatever you ask of me, I will give you, up to half my kingdom!”",
"006:024 Then she went out and asked her mother, “What should I request?” And her mother answered, “The head of John the Baptist.”",
"006:025 At once the girl hurried back to the king with her request: “I want you to give me the head of John the Baptist on a platter immediately.”",
"006:026 The king was consumed with sorrow, but because of his oaths and his guests, he did not want to refuse her.",
"006:027 So without delay, the king commanded that John’s head be brought in. He sent an executioner, who went and beheaded him in the prison.",
"006:028 The man brought John’s head on a platter and presented it to the girl, who gave it to her mother.",
"006:029 When John’s disciples heard about this, they came and took his body and placed it in a tomb.",
"006:030 Meanwhile, the apostles gathered around Jesus and brought Him news of all they had done and taught.",
"006:031 And He said to them, “Come with Me privately to a solitary place, and let us rest for a while.” For many people were coming and going, and they did not even have time to eat.",
"006:032 So they went away in a boat by themselves to a solitary place.",
"006:033 But many people saw them leaving and recognized them. They ran together on foot from all the towns and arrived before them.",
"006:034 When Jesus stepped ashore and saw a large crowd, He had compassion on them, because they were like sheep without a shepherd. And He began to teach them many things.",
"006:035 By now the hour was already late. So the disciples came to Jesus and said, “This is a desolate place, and the hour is already late.",
"006:036 Dismiss the crowd so they can go to the surrounding countryside and villages and buy themselves something to eat.”",
"006:037 But Jesus told them, “You give them something to eat.” They asked Him, “Should we go out and spend two hundred denarii to give all of them bread to eat?”",
"006:038 “Go and see how many loaves you have,” He told them. And after checking, they said, “Five—and two fish.”",
"006:039 Then Jesus directed them to have the people sit in groups on the green grass.",
"006:040 So they sat down in groups of hundreds and fifties.",
"006:041 Taking the five loaves and the two fish and looking up to heaven, Jesus spoke a blessing and broke the loaves. Then He gave them to His disciples to set before the people. And He divided the two fish among them all.",
"006:042 They all ate and were satisfied,",
"006:043 and the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces of bread and fish.",
"006:044 And there were five thousand men who had eaten the loaves.",
"006:045 Immediately Jesus made His disciples get into the boat and go on ahead of Him to Bethsaida, while He dismissed the crowd.",
"006:046 After bidding them farewell, He went up on the mountain to pray.",
"006:047 When evening came, the boat was in the middle of the sea, and Jesus was alone on land.",
"006:048 He could see that the disciples were straining to row, because the wind was against them. About the fourth watch of the night, Jesus went out to them, walking on the sea. He intended to pass by them,",
"006:049 but when they saw Him walking on the sea, they cried out, thinking He was a ghost—",
"006:050 for they all saw Him and were terrified. But Jesus spoke up at once: “Take courage! It is I. Do not be afraid.”",
"006:051 Then He climbed into the boat with them, and the wind died down. And the disciples were utterly astounded,",
"006:052 for they had not understood about the loaves, but their hearts had been hardened.",
"006:053 When they had crossed over, they landed at Gennesaret and moored the boat.",
"006:054 As soon as they got out of the boat, the people recognized Jesus",
"006:055 and ran through that whole region, carrying the sick on mats to wherever they heard He was.",
"006:056 And wherever He went—villages and towns and countrysides—they laid the sick in the marketplaces and begged Him just to let them touch the fringe of His cloak. And all who touched Him were healed."
],
[
"007:001 Then the Pharisees and some of the scribes who had come from Jerusalem gathered around Jesus,",
"007:002 and they saw some of His disciples eating with hands that were defiled—that is, unwashed.",
"007:003 Now in holding to the tradition of the elders, the Pharisees and all the Jews do not eat until they wash their hands ceremonially.",
"007:004 And on returning from the market, they do not eat unless they wash. And there are many other traditions for them to observe, including the washing of cups, pitchers, kettles, and couches for dining.",
"007:005 So the Pharisees and scribes questioned Jesus: “Why do Your disciples not walk according to the tradition of the elders? Instead, they eat with defiled hands.”",
"007:006 Jesus answered them, “Isaiah prophesied correctly about you hypocrites, as it is written: ‘These people honor Me with their lips, but their hearts are far from Me.",
"007:007 They worship Me in vain; they teach as doctrine the precepts of men.’",
"007:008 You have disregarded the commandment of God to keep the tradition of men.”",
"007:009 He went on to say, “You neatly set aside the command of God to maintain your own tradition.",
"007:010 For Moses said, ‘Honor your father and your mother’ and ‘Anyone who curses his father or mother must be put to death.’",
"007:011 But you say that if a man says to his father or mother, ‘Whatever you would have received from me is Corban’ (that is, a gift devoted to God),",
"007:012 he is no longer permitted to do anything for his father or mother.",
"007:013 Thus you nullify the word of God by the tradition you have handed down. And you do so in many such matters.”",
"007:014 Once again Jesus called the crowd to Him and said, “All of you, listen to Me and understand:",
"007:015 Nothing that enters a man from the outside can defile him; but the things that come out of a man, these are what defile him.”",
"007:016 OMITTED TEXT",
"007:017 After Jesus had left the crowd and gone into the house, His disciples inquired about the parable.",
"007:018 “Are you still so dull?” He asked. “Do you not understand? Nothing that enters a man from the outside can defile him,",
"007:019 because it does not enter his heart, but it goes into the stomach and then is eliminated.” (Thus all foods are clean.)",
"007:020 He continued: “What comes out of a man, that is what defiles him.",
"007:021 For from within the hearts of men come evil thoughts, sexual immorality, theft, murder, adultery,",
"007:022 greed, wickedness, deceit, debauchery, envy, slander, arrogance, and foolishness.",
"007:023 All these evils come from within, and these are what defile a man.”",
"007:024 Jesus left that place and went to the region of Tyre. Not wanting anyone to know He was there, He entered a house, but was unable to escape their notice.",
"007:025 Instead, a woman whose little daughter had an unclean spirit soon heard about Jesus, and she came and fell at His feet.",
"007:026 Now she was a Greek woman of Syrophoenician origin, and she kept asking Jesus to drive the demon out of her daughter.",
"007:027 “First let the children have their fill,” He said. “For it is not right to take the children’s bread and toss it to the dogs.”",
"007:028 “Yes, Lord,” she replied, “even the dogs under the table eat the children’s crumbs.”",
"007:029 Then Jesus told her, “Because of this answer, you may go. The demon has left your daughter.”",
"007:030 And she went home and found her child lying on the bed, and the demon was gone.",
"007:031 Then Jesus left the region of Tyre and went through Sidon to the Sea of Galilee and into the region of the Decapolis.",
"007:032 Some people brought to Him a man who was deaf and hardly able to speak, and they begged Jesus to place His hand on him.",
"007:033 So Jesus took him aside privately, away from the crowd, and put His fingers into the man’s ears. Then He spit and touched the man’s tongue.",
"007:034 And looking up to heaven, He sighed deeply and said to him, “Ephphatha!” (which means, “Be opened!”).",
"007:035 Immediately the man’s ears were opened and his tongue was released, and he began to speak plainly.",
"007:036 Jesus ordered them not to tell anyone. But the more He ordered them, the more widely they proclaimed it.",
"007:037 The people were utterly astonished and said, “He has done all things well! He makes even the deaf hear and the mute speak!”"
],
[
"008:001 In those days the crowd once again became very large, and they had nothing to eat. Jesus called the disciples to Him and said,",
"008:002 “I have compassion for this crowd, because they have already been with Me three days and have nothing to eat.",
"008:003 If I send them home hungry, they will faint along the way. For some of them have come a great distance.”",
"008:004 His disciples replied, “Where in this desolate place could anyone find enough bread to feed all these people?”",
"008:005 “How many loaves do you have?” Jesus asked. “Seven,” they replied.",
"008:006 And He instructed the crowd to sit down on the ground. Then He took the seven loaves, gave thanks and broke them, and gave them to His disciples to set before the people. And they distributed them to the crowd.",
"008:007 They also had a few small fish, and Jesus blessed them and ordered that these be set before them as well.",
"008:008 The people ate and were satisfied, and the disciples picked up seven basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over.",
"008:009 And about four thousand men were present. And when Jesus had dismissed the crowd,",
"008:010 He immediately got into the boat with His disciples and went to the district of Dalmanutha.",
"008:011 Then the Pharisees came and began to argue with Jesus, testing Him by demanding from Him a sign from heaven.",
"008:012 Jesus sighed deeply in His spirit and said, “Why does this generation demand a sign? Truly I tell you, no sign will be given to this generation.”",
"008:013 And He left them, got back into the boat, and crossed to the other side.",
"008:014 Now the disciples had forgotten to take bread, except for one loaf they had with them in the boat.",
"008:015 “Watch out!” He cautioned them. “Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of Herod.”",
"008:016 So they began to discuss with one another the fact that they had no bread.",
"008:017 Aware of their conversation, Jesus asked them, “Why are you debating about having no bread? Do you still not see or understand? Do you have such hard hearts?",
"008:018 ‘Having eyes, do you not see? And having ears, do you not hear?’ And do you not remember?",
"008:019 When I broke the five loaves for the five thousand, how many basketfuls of broken pieces did you collect?” “Twelve,” they answered.",
"008:020 “And when I broke the seven loaves for the four thousand, how many basketfuls of broken pieces did you collect?” “Seven,” they said.",
"008:021 Then He asked them, “Do you still not understand?”",
"008:022 When they arrived at Bethsaida, some people brought a blind man and begged Jesus to touch him.",
"008:023 So He took the blind man by the hand and led him out of the village. Then He spit on the man’s eyes and placed His hands on him. “Can you see anything?” He asked.",
"008:024 The man looked up and said, “I can see the people, but they look like trees walking around.”",
"008:025 Once again Jesus placed His hands on the man’s eyes, and when he opened them his sight was restored, and he could see everything clearly.",
"008:026 Jesus sent him home and said, “Do not go back into the village.”",
"008:027 Then Jesus and His disciples went on to the villages around Caesarea Philippi. On the way, He questioned His disciples: “Who do people say I am?”",
"008:028 They replied, “Some say John the Baptist; others say Elijah; and still others, one of the prophets.”",
"008:029 “But what about you?” Jesus asked. “Who do you say I am?” Peter answered, “You are the Christ.”",
"008:030 And Jesus warned them not to tell anyone about Him.",
"008:031 Then He began to teach them that the Son of Man must suffer many things and be rejected by the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and that He must be killed and after three days rise again.",
"008:032 He spoke this message quite frankly, and Peter took Him aside and began to rebuke Him.",
"008:033 But Jesus, turning and looking at His disciples, rebuked Peter and said, “Get behind Me, Satan! For you do not have in mind the things of God, but the things of men.”",
"008:034 Then Jesus called the crowd to Him along with His disciples, and He told them, “If anyone wants to come after Me, he must deny himself and take up his cross and follow Me.",
"008:035 For whoever wants to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life for My sake and for the gospel will save it.",
"008:036 What does it profit a man to gain the whole world, yet forfeit his soul?",
"008:037 Or what can a man give in exchange for his soul?",
"008:038 If anyone is ashamed of Me and My words in this adulterous and sinful generation, the Son of Man will also be ashamed of him when He comes in His Father’s glory with the holy angels.”"
],
[
"009:001 Then Jesus said to them, “Truly I tell you, there are some standing here who will not taste death before they see the kingdom of God arrive with power.”",
"009:002 After six days Jesus took with Him Peter, James, and John, and led them up a high mountain by themselves. There He was transfigured before them.",
"009:003 His clothes became radiantly white, brighter than any launderer on earth could bleach them.",
"009:004 And Elijah and Moses appeared before them, talking with Jesus.",
"009:005 Peter said to Jesus, “Rabbi, it is good for us to be here. Let us put up three shelters—one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.”",
"009:006 For they were all so terrified that Peter did not know what else to say.",
"009:007 Then a cloud appeared and enveloped them, and a voice came from the cloud: “This is My beloved Son. Listen to Him!”",
"009:008 Suddenly, when they looked around, they saw no one with them except Jesus.",
"009:009 As they were coming down the mountain, Jesus admonished them not to tell anyone what they had seen until the Son of Man had risen from the dead.",
"009:010 So they kept this matter to themselves, discussing what it meant to rise from the dead.",
"009:011 And they asked Jesus, “Why do the scribes say that Elijah must come first?”",
"009:012 He replied, “Elijah does indeed come first, and he restores all things. Why then is it written that the Son of Man must suffer many things and be rejected?",
"009:013 But I tell you that Elijah has indeed come, and they have done to him whatever they wished, just as it is written about him.”",
"009:014 When they returned to the other disciples, they saw a large crowd around them, and scribes arguing with them.",
"009:015 As soon as all the people saw Jesus, they were filled with awe and ran to greet Him.",
"009:016 “What are you disputing with them?” He asked.",
"009:017 Someone in the crowd replied, “Teacher, I brought You my son, who has a spirit that makes him mute.",
"009:018 Whenever it seizes him, it throws him to the ground. He foams at the mouth, gnashes his teeth, and becomes rigid. I asked Your disciples to drive it out, but they were unable.”",
"009:019 “O unbelieving generation!” Jesus replied. “How long must I remain with you? How long must I put up with you? Bring the boy to Me.”",
"009:020 So they brought him, and seeing Jesus, the spirit immediately threw the boy into a convulsion. He fell to the ground and rolled around, foaming at the mouth.",
"009:021 Jesus asked the boy’s father, “How long has this been with him?” “From childhood,” he said.",
"009:022 “It often throws him into the fire or into the water, trying to kill him. But if You can do anything, have compassion on us and help us.”",
"009:023 “If You can?” echoed Jesus. “All things are possible to him who believes!”",
"009:024 Immediately the boy’s father cried out, “I do believe; help my unbelief!”",
"009:025 When Jesus saw that a crowd had come running, He rebuked the unclean spirit. “You deaf and mute spirit,” He said, “I command you to come out and never enter him again.”",
"009:026 After shrieking and convulsing him violently, the spirit came out. The boy became like a corpse, so that many said, “He is dead.”",
"009:027 But Jesus took him by the hand and helped him to his feet, and he stood up.",
"009:028 After Jesus had gone into the house, His disciples asked Him privately, “Why couldn’t we drive it out?”",
"009:029 Jesus answered, “This kind cannot come out, except by prayer.”",
"009:030 Going on from there, they passed through Galilee. But Jesus did not want anyone to know,",
"009:031 because He was teaching His disciples. He told them, “The Son of Man will be delivered into the hands of men. They will kill Him, and after three days He will rise.”",
"009:032 But they did not understand this statement, and they were afraid to ask Him about it.",
"009:033 Then they came to Capernaum. While Jesus was in the house, He asked them, “What were you discussing on the way?”",
"009:034 But they were silent, for on the way they had been arguing about which of them was the greatest.",
"009:035 Sitting down, Jesus called the Twelve and said, “If anyone wants to be first, he must be the last of all and the servant of all.”",
"009:036 Then He had a little child stand among them. Taking the child in His arms, He said to them,",
"009:037 “Whoever welcomes one of these little children in My name welcomes Me, and whoever welcomes Me welcomes not only Me, but the One who sent Me.”",
"009:038 John said to Him, “Teacher, we saw someone else driving out demons in Your name, and we tried to stop him, because he does not accompany us.”",
"009:039 “Do not stop him,” Jesus replied. “For no one who performs a miracle in My name can turn around and speak evil of Me.",
"009:040 For whoever is not against us is for us.",
"009:041 Indeed, if anyone gives you even a cup of water because you bear the name of Christ, truly I tell you, he will never lose his reward.",
"009:042 But if anyone causes one of these little ones who believe in Me to stumble, it would be better for him to have a large millstone hung around his neck and to be thrown into the sea.",
"009:043 If your hand causes you to sin, cut it off. It is better for you to enter life crippled than to have two hands and go into hell, into the unquenchable fire.",
"009:044 OMITTED TEXT",
"009:045 If your foot causes you to sin, cut it off. It is better for you to enter life lame than to have two feet and be thrown into hell.",
"009:046 OMITTED TEXT",
"009:047 And if your eye causes you to sin, pluck it out. It is better for you to enter the kingdom of God with one eye than to have two eyes and be thrown into hell,",
"009:048 where ‘their worm never dies, and the fire is never quenched.’",
"009:049 For everyone will be salted with fire.",
"009:050 Salt is good, but if the salt loses its saltiness, with what will you season it? Have salt among yourselves, and be at peace with one another.”"
],
[
"010:001 Then Jesus left that place and went into the region of Judea, beyond the Jordan. Again the crowds came to Him and He taught them, as was His custom.",
"010:002 Some Pharisees came to test Him. “Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife?” they inquired.",
"010:003 “What did Moses command you?” He replied.",
"010:004 They answered, “Moses permitted a man to write his wife a certificate of divorce and send her away.”",
"010:005 But Jesus told them, “Moses wrote this commandment for you because of your hardness of heart.",
"010:006 However, from the beginning of creation, ‘God made them male and female.’",
"010:007 ‘For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife,",
"010:008 and the two will become one flesh.’ So they are no longer two, but one flesh.",
"010:009 Therefore what God has joined together, let man not separate.”",
"010:010 When they were back inside the house, the disciples asked Jesus about this matter.",
"010:011 So He told them, “Whoever divorces his wife and marries another woman commits adultery against her.",
"010:012 And if a woman divorces her husband and marries another man, she commits adultery.”",
"010:013 Now people were bringing the little children to Jesus for Him to place His hands on them, and the disciples rebuked those who brought them.",
"010:014 But when Jesus saw this, He was indignant and told them, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not hinder them! For the kingdom of God belongs to such as these.",
"010:015 Truly I tell you, anyone who does not receive the kingdom of God like a little child will never enter it.”",
"010:016 And He took the children in His arms, placed His hands on them, and blessed them.",
"010:017 As Jesus started on His way, a man ran up and knelt before Him. “Good Teacher,” he asked, “what must I do to inherit eternal life?”",
"010:018 “Why do you call Me good?” Jesus replied. “No one is good except God alone.",
"010:019 You know the commandments: ‘Do not murder, do not commit adultery, do not steal, do not bear false witness, do not cheat others, honor your father and mother.’”",
"010:020 “Teacher,” he replied, “all these I have kept from my youth.”",
"010:021 Jesus looked at him, loved him, and said to him, “There is one thing you lack: Go, sell everything you own and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven. Then come, follow Me.”",
"010:022 But the man was saddened by these words and went away in sorrow, because he had great wealth.",
"010:023 Then Jesus looked around and said to His disciples, “How hard it is for the rich to enter the kingdom of God!”",
"010:024 And the disciples were amazed at His words. But Jesus said to them again, “Children, how hard it is to enter the kingdom of God!",
"010:025 It is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God.”",
"010:026 They were even more astonished and said to one another, “Who then can be saved?”",
"010:027 Jesus looked at them and said, “With man this is impossible, but not with God. For all things are possible with God.”",
"010:028 Peter began to say to Him, “Look, we have left everything and followed You.”",
"010:029 “Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “no one who has left home or brothers or sisters or mother or father or children or fields for My sake and for the gospel",
"010:030 will fail to receive a hundredfold in the present age—houses and brothers and sisters and mothers and children and fields, along with persecutions—and in the age to come, eternal life.",
"010:031 But many who are first will be last, and the last will be first.”",
"010:032 As they were going up the road to Jerusalem, Jesus was walking ahead of them. The disciples were amazed, but those who followed were afraid. Again Jesus took the Twelve aside and began to tell them what was going to happen to Him:",
"010:033 “Look, we are going up to Jerusalem, and the Son of Man will be delivered over to the chief priests and scribes. They will condemn Him to death and will deliver Him over to the Gentiles,",
"010:034 who will mock Him and spit on Him and flog Him and kill Him. And after three days He will rise again.”",
"010:035 Then James and John, the sons of Zebedee, came to Jesus and declared, “Teacher, we want You to do for us whatever we ask.”",
"010:036 “What do you want Me to do for you?” He inquired.",
"010:037 They answered, “Grant that one of us may sit at Your right hand and the other at Your left in Your glory.”",
"010:038 “You do not know what you are asking,” Jesus replied. “Can you drink the cup I will drink, or be baptized with the baptism I will undergo?”",
"010:039 “We can,” the brothers answered. “You will drink the cup that I drink,” Jesus said, “and you will be baptized with the baptism that I undergo.",
"010:040 But to sit at My right or left is not Mine to grant. These seats belong to those for whom they have been prepared.”",
"010:041 When the ten heard about this, they became indignant with James and John.",
"010:042 So Jesus called them together and said, “You know that those regarded as rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and their superiors exercise authority over them.",
"010:043 But it shall not be this way among you. Instead, whoever wants to become great among you must be your servant,",
"010:044 and whoever wants to be first must be the slave of all.",
"010:045 For even the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give His life as a ransom for many.”",
"010:046 Next, they came to Jericho. And as Jesus and His disciples were leaving Jericho with a large crowd, a blind beggar named Bartimaeus, the son of Timaeus, was sitting beside the road.",
"010:047 When he heard that it was Jesus of Nazareth, he began to cry out, “Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!”",
"010:048 Many people admonished him to be silent, but he cried out all the louder, “Son of David, have mercy on me!”",
"010:049 Jesus stopped and said, “Call him.” So they called the blind man. “Take courage!” they said. “Get up! He is calling for you.”",
"010:050 Throwing off his cloak, Bartimaeus jumped up and came to Jesus.",
"010:051 “What do you want Me to do for you?” Jesus asked. “Rabboni,” said the blind man, “let me see again.”",
"010:052 “Go,” said Jesus, “your faith has healed you.” And immediately he received his sight and followed Jesus along the road."
],
[
"011:001 As they approached Jerusalem and came to Bethphage and Bethany at the Mount of Olives, Jesus sent out two of His disciples",
"011:002 and said to them, “Go into the village ahead of you, and as soon as you enter it, you will find a colt tied there, on which no one has ever sat. Untie it and bring it here.",
"011:003 If anyone asks, ‘Why are you doing this?’ tell him, ‘The Lord needs it and will return it shortly.’”",
"011:004 So they went and found the colt outside in the street, tied at a doorway. They untied it,",
"011:005 and some who were standing there asked, “Why are you untying the colt?”",
"011:006 The disciples answered as Jesus had instructed them, and the people gave them permission.",
"011:007 Then they led the colt to Jesus and threw their cloaks over it, and He sat on it.",
"011:008 Many in the crowd spread their cloaks on the road, while others spread branches they had cut from the fields.",
"011:009 The ones who went ahead and those who followed were shouting: “Hosanna!” “Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!”",
"011:010 “Blessed is the coming kingdom of our father David!” “Hosanna in the highest!”",
"011:011 Then Jesus entered Jerusalem and went into the temple courts. He looked around at everything, but since it was already late, He went out to Bethany with the Twelve.",
"011:012 The next day, when they had left Bethany, Jesus was hungry.",
"011:013 Seeing in the distance a fig tree in leaf, He went to see if there was any fruit on it. But when He reached it, He found nothing on it except leaves, since it was not the season for figs.",
"011:014 Then He said to the tree, “May no one ever eat of your fruit again.” And His disciples heard this statement.",
"011:015 When they arrived in Jerusalem, Jesus entered the temple courts and began to drive out those who were buying and selling there. He overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those selling doves.",
"011:016 And He would not allow anyone to carry merchandise through the temple courts.",
"011:017 Then Jesus began to teach them, and He declared, “Is it not written: ‘My house will be called a house of prayer for all the nations’? But you have made it ‘a den of robbers.’”",
"011:018 When the chief priests and scribes heard this, they looked for a way to kill Him. For they were afraid of Him, because the whole crowd was astonished at His teaching.",
"011:019 And when evening came, Jesus and His disciples went out of the city.",
"011:020 As they were walking back in the morning, they saw the fig tree withered from its roots.",
"011:021 Peter remembered it and said, “Look, Rabbi! The fig tree You cursed has withered.”",
"011:022 “Have faith in God,” Jesus said to them.",
"011:023 “Truly I tell you that if anyone says to this mountain, ‘Be lifted up and thrown into the sea,’ and has no doubt in his heart but believes that it will happen, it will be done for him.",
"011:024 Therefore I tell you, whatever you ask for in prayer, believe that you have received it, and it will be yours.",
"011:025 And when you stand to pray, if you hold anything against another, forgive it, so that your Father in heaven will forgive your trespasses as well.”",
"011:026 OMITTED TEXT",
"011:027 After their return to Jerusalem, Jesus was walking in the temple courts, and the chief priests, scribes, and elders came up to Him.",
"011:028 “By what authority are You doing these things?” they asked. “And who gave You the authority to do them?”",
"011:029 “I will ask you one question,” Jesus replied, “and if you answer Me, I will tell you by what authority I am doing these things.",
"011:030 John’s baptism—was it from heaven or from men? Answer Me!”",
"011:031 They deliberated among themselves what they should answer: “If we say, ‘From heaven,’ He will ask, ‘Why then did you not believe him?’",
"011:032 But if we say, ‘From men’...” they were afraid of the people, for they all held that John truly was a prophet.",
"011:033 So they answered, “We do not know.” And Jesus replied, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I am doing these things.”"
],
[
"012:001 Then Jesus began to speak to them in parables: “A man planted a vineyard. He put a wall around it, dug a wine vat, and built a watchtower. Then he rented it out to some tenants and went away on a journey.",
"012:002 At harvest time, he sent a servant to the tenants to collect his share of the fruit of the vineyard.",
"012:003 But they seized the servant, beat him, and sent him away empty-handed.",
"012:004 Then he sent them another servant, and they struck him over the head and treated him shamefully.",
"012:005 He sent still another, and this one they killed. He sent many others; some they beat and others they killed.",
"012:006 Finally, having one beloved son, he sent him to them. ‘They will respect my son,’ he said.",
"012:007 But the tenants said to one another, ‘This is the heir. Come, let us kill him, and the inheritance will be ours.’",
"012:008 So they seized the son, killed him, and threw him out of the vineyard.",
"012:009 What then will the owner of the vineyard do? He will come and kill those tenants and give the vineyard to others.",
"012:010 Have you never read this Scripture: ‘The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone.",
"012:011 This is from the Lord, and it is marvelous in our eyes’?”",
"012:012 At this, the leaders sought to arrest Jesus, for they knew that He had spoken this parable against them. But fearing the crowd, they left Him and went away.",
"012:013 Later, they sent some of the Pharisees and Herodians to catch Jesus in His words.",
"012:014 “Teacher,” they said, “we know that You are honest and seek favor from no one. Indeed, You are impartial and teach the way of God in accordance with the truth. Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar or not? Should we pay them or not?”",
"012:015 But Jesus saw through their hypocrisy and said, “Why are you testing Me? Bring Me a denarius to inspect.”",
"012:016 So they brought it, and He asked them, “Whose image is this? And whose inscription?” “Caesar’s,” they answered.",
"012:017 Then Jesus told them, “Give to Caesar what is Caesar’s, and to God what is God’s.” And they marveled at Him.",
"012:018 Then the Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection, came to Jesus and questioned Him:",
"012:019 “Teacher, Moses wrote for us that if a man’s brother dies and leaves a wife but no children, the man is to marry his brother’s widow and raise up offspring for him.",
"012:020 Now there were seven brothers. The first one married and died, leaving no children.",
"012:021 Then the second one married the widow, but he also died and left no children. And the third did likewise.",
"012:022 In this way, none of the seven left any children. And last of all, the woman died.",
"012:023 In the resurrection, then, whose wife will she be? For all seven were married to her.”",
"012:024 Jesus said to them, “Aren’t you mistaken, because you do not know the Scriptures or the power of God?",
"012:025 When the dead rise, they will neither marry nor be given in marriage. Instead, they will be like the angels in heaven.",
"012:026 But concerning the dead rising, have you not read about the burning bush in the Book of Moses, how God told him, ‘I am the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob’?",
"012:027 He is not the God of the dead, but of the living. You are badly mistaken!”",
"012:028 Now one of the scribes had come up and heard their debate. Noticing how well Jesus had answered them, he asked Him, “Which commandment is the most important of all?”",
"012:029 Jesus replied, “This is the most important: ‘Hear O Israel, the Lord our God, the Lord is One.",
"012:030 Love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your mind and with all your strength.’",
"012:031 The second is this: ‘Love your neighbor as yourself.’ No other commandment is greater than these.”",
"012:032 “Right, Teacher,” the scribe replied. “You have stated correctly that God is One and there is no other but Him,",
"012:033 and to love Him with all your heart and with all your understanding and with all your strength, and to love your neighbor as yourself. This is more important than all burnt offerings and sacrifices.”",
"012:034 When Jesus saw that the man had answered wisely, He said, “You are not far from the kingdom of God.” And no one dared to question Him any further.",
"012:035 While Jesus was teaching in the temple courts, He asked, “How can the scribes say that the Christ is the Son of David?",
"012:036 Speaking by the Holy Spirit, David himself declared: ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand until I put Your enemies under Your feet.”’",
"012:037 David himself calls Him ‘Lord.’ So how can He be David’s son?” And the large crowd listened to Him with delight.",
"012:038 In His teaching Jesus also said, “Watch out for the scribes. They like to walk around in long robes, to receive greetings in the marketplaces,",
"012:039 and to have the chief seats in the synagogues and the places of honor at banquets.",
"012:040 They defraud widows of their houses, and for a show make lengthy prayers. These men will receive greater condemnation.”",
"012:041 As Jesus was sitting opposite the treasury, He watched the crowd putting money into it. And many rich people put in large amounts.",
"012:042 Then one poor widow came and put in two small copper coins, which amounted to a small fraction of a denarius.",
"012:043 Jesus called His disciples to Him and said, “Truly I tell you, this poor widow has put more than all the others into the treasury.",
"012:044 For they all contributed out of their surplus, but she out of her poverty has put in all she had to live on.”"
],
[
"013:001 As Jesus was leaving the temple, one of His disciples said to Him, “Teacher, look at the magnificent stones and buildings!”",
"013:002 “Do you see all these great buildings?” Jesus replied. “Not one stone here will be left on another; every one will be thrown down.”",
"013:003 While Jesus was sitting on the Mount of Olives opposite the temple, Peter, James, John, and Andrew asked Him privately,",
"013:004 “Tell us, when will these things happen? And what will be the sign that they are about to be fulfilled?”",
"013:005 Jesus began by telling them, “See to it that no one deceives you.",
"013:006 Many will come in My name, claiming, ‘I am He,’ and will deceive many.",
"013:007 When you hear of wars and rumors of wars, do not be alarmed. These things must happen, but the end is still to come.",
"013:008 Nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom. There will be earthquakes in various places, as well as famines. These are the beginning of birth pains.",
"013:009 So be on your guard. You will be delivered over to the councils and beaten in the synagogues. On My account you will stand before governors and kings as witnesses to them.",
"013:010 And the gospel must first be proclaimed to all the nations.",
"013:011 But when they arrest you and hand you over, do not worry beforehand what to say. Instead, speak whatever you are given at that time, for it will not be you speaking, but the Holy Spirit.",
"013:012 Brother will betray brother to death, and a father his child. Children will rise against their parents and have them put to death.",
"013:013 You will be hated by everyone because of My name, but the one who perseveres to the end will be saved.",
"013:014 So when you see the abomination of desolation standing where it should not be (let the reader understand), then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains.",
"013:015 Let no one on the housetop go back inside to retrieve anything from his house.",
"013:016 And let no one in the field return for his cloak.",
"013:017 How miserable those days will be for pregnant and nursing mothers!",
"013:018 Pray that this will not occur in the winter.",
"013:019 For those will be days of tribulation unseen from the beginning of God’s creation until now, and never to be seen again.",
"013:020 If the Lord had not cut short those days, nobody would be saved. But for the sake of the elect, whom He has chosen, He has cut them short.",
"013:021 At that time if anyone says to you, ‘Look, here is the Christ!’ or ‘There He is!’ do not believe it.",
"013:022 For false Christs and false prophets will appear and perform signs and wonders to deceive even the elect, if that were possible.",
"013:023 So be on your guard; I have told you everything in advance.",
"013:024 But in those days, after that tribulation: ‘The sun will be darkened, and the moon will not give its light;",
"013:025 the stars will fall from the sky, and the powers of the heavens will be shaken.’",
"013:026 At that time they will see the Son of Man coming in the clouds with great power and glory.",
"013:027 And He will send out the angels to gather His elect from the four winds, from the ends of the earth to the ends of heaven.",
"013:028 Now learn this lesson from the fig tree: As soon as its branches become tender and sprout leaves, you know that summer is near.",
"013:029 So also, when you see these things happening, know that He is near, right at the door.",
"013:030 Truly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all these things have happened.",
"013:031 Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away.",
"013:032 No one knows about that day or hour, not even the angels in heaven, nor the Son, but only the Father.",
"013:033 Be on your guard and stay alert! For you do not know when the appointed time will come.",
"013:034 It is like a man going on a journey who left his house, put each servant in charge of his own task, and instructed the doorkeeper to keep watch.",
"013:035 Therefore keep watch, because you do not know when the master of the house will return—whether in the evening, at midnight, when the rooster crows, or in the morning.",
"013:036 Otherwise, he may arrive without notice and find you sleeping.",
"013:037 And what I say to you, I say to everyone: Keep watch!”"
],
[
"014:001 Now the Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread were two days away, and the chief priests and scribes were looking for a covert way to arrest Jesus and kill Him.",
"014:002 “But not during the feast,” they said, “or there may be a riot among the people.”",
"014:003 While Jesus was in Bethany reclining at the table in the home of Simon the Leper, a woman came with an alabaster jar of expensive perfume, made of pure nard. She broke open the jar and poured it on Jesus’ head.",
"014:004 Some of those present, however, expressed their indignation to one another: “Why this waste of perfume?",
"014:005 It could have been sold for over three hundred denarii and the money given to the poor.” And they scolded her.",
"014:006 But Jesus said, “Leave her alone; why are you bothering her? She has done a beautiful deed to Me.",
"014:007 The poor you will always have with you, and you can help them whenever you want. But you will not always have Me.",
"014:008 She has done what she could to anoint My body in advance of My burial.",
"014:009 And truly I tell you, wherever the gospel is preached in all the world, what she has done will also be told in memory of her.”",
"014:010 Then Judas Iscariot, one of the Twelve, went to the chief priests to betray Jesus to them.",
"014:011 They were delighted to hear this, and they promised to give him money. So Judas began to look for an opportunity to betray Jesus.",
"014:012 On the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread, when the Passover lamb was to be sacrificed, Jesus’ disciples asked Him, “Where do You want us to prepare for You to eat the Passover?”",
"014:013 So He sent two of His disciples and told them, “Go into the city, and a man carrying a jug of water will meet you. Follow him,",
"014:014 and whichever house he enters, say to the owner, ‘The Teacher asks: Where is My guest room, where I may eat the Passover with My disciples?’",
"014:015 And he will show you a large upper room, furnished and ready. Make preparations for us there.”",
"014:016 So the disciples left and went into the city, where they found everything as Jesus had described. And they prepared the Passover.",
"014:017 When evening came, Jesus arrived with the Twelve.",
"014:018 And while they were reclining and eating, Jesus said, “Truly I tell you, one of you who is eating with Me will betray Me.”",
"014:019 They began to be grieved and to ask Him one after another, “Surely not I?”",
"014:020 He answered, “It is one of the Twelve—the one who is dipping his hand into the bowl with Me.",
"014:021 The Son of Man will go just as it is written about Him, but woe to that man by whom He is betrayed! It would be better for him if he had not been born.”",
"014:022 While they were eating, Jesus took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to the disciples, saying, “Take it; this is My body.”",
"014:023 Then He took the cup, gave thanks, and gave it to them, and they all drank from it.",
"014:024 He said to them, “This is My blood of the covenant, which is poured out for many.",
"014:025 Truly I tell you, I will no longer drink of the fruit of the vine until that day when I drink it anew in the kingdom of God.”",
"014:026 And when they had sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives.",
"014:027 Then Jesus said to them, “You will all fall away, for it is written: ‘I will strike the Shepherd, and the sheep will be scattered.’",
"014:028 But after I have risen, I will go ahead of you into Galilee.”",
"014:029 Peter declared, “Even if all fall away, I never will.”",
"014:030 “Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “this very night, before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.”",
"014:031 But Peter kept insisting, “Even if I have to die with You, I will never deny You.” And all the others said the same thing.",
"014:032 Then they came to a place called Gethsemane, and Jesus told His disciples, “Sit here while I pray.”",
"014:033 He took with Him Peter, James, and John, and began to be deeply troubled and distressed.",
"014:034 Then He said to them, “My soul is consumed with sorrow to the point of death. Stay here and keep watch.”",
"014:035 Going a little farther, He fell to the ground and prayed that, if it were possible, the hour would pass from Him.",
"014:036 “Abba, Father,” He said, “all things are possible for You. Take this cup from Me. Yet not what I will, but what You will.”",
"014:037 Then Jesus returned and found them sleeping. “Simon, are you asleep?” He asked. “Were you not able to keep watch for one hour?",
"014:038 Watch and pray so that you will not enter into temptation. For the spirit is willing, but the body is weak.”",
"014:039 Again He went away and prayed, saying the same thing.",
"014:040 And again Jesus returned and found them sleeping, for their eyes were heavy. And they did not know what to answer Him.",
"014:041 When Jesus returned the third time, He said, “Are you still sleeping and resting? That is enough! The hour has come. Look, the Son of Man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.",
"014:042 Rise, let us go. See, My betrayer is approaching!”",
"014:043 While Jesus was still speaking, Judas, one of the Twelve, arrived, accompanied by a crowd armed with swords and clubs, sent from the chief priests, scribes, and elders.",
"014:044 Now the betrayer had arranged a signal with them: “The One I kiss is the man; arrest Him and lead Him away securely.”",
"014:045 Going directly to Jesus, he said, “Rabbi!” and kissed Him.",
"014:046 Then the men seized Jesus and arrested Him.",
"014:047 And one of the bystanders drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his ear.",
"014:048 Jesus asked the crowd, “Have you come out with swords and clubs to arrest Me as you would an outlaw?",
"014:049 Every day I was with you, teaching in the temple courts, and you did not arrest Me. But this has happened that the Scriptures would be fulfilled.”",
"014:050 Then everyone deserted Him and fled.",
"014:051 One young man who had been following Jesus was wearing a linen cloth around his body. They caught hold of him,",
"014:052 but he pulled free of the linen cloth and ran away naked.",
"014:053 They led Jesus away to the high priest, and all the chief priests, elders, and scribes assembled.",
"014:054 Peter followed Him at a distance, right into the courtyard of the high priest. And he sat with the officers and warmed himself by the fire.",
"014:055 Now the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin were seeking testimony against Jesus to put Him to death, but they did not find any.",
"014:056 For many bore false witness against Jesus, but their testimony was inconsistent.",
"014:057 Then some men stood up and testified falsely against Him:",
"014:058 “We heard Him say, ‘I will destroy this man-made temple, and in three days I will build another that is made without hands.’”",
"014:059 But even their testimony was inconsistent.",
"014:060 So the high priest stood up before them and questioned Jesus, “Have You no answer? What are these men testifying against You?”",
"014:061 But Jesus remained silent and made no reply. Again the high priest questioned Him, “Are You the Christ, the Son of the Blessed One?”",
"014:062 “I am,” said Jesus, “and you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of Power and coming with the clouds of heaven.”",
"014:063 At this, the high priest tore his clothes and declared, “Why do we need any more witnesses?",
"014:064 You have heard the blasphemy. What is your verdict?” And they all condemned Him as deserving of death.",
"014:065 Then some of them began to spit on Him. They blindfolded Him, struck Him with their fists, and said to Him, “Prophesy!” And the officers received Him with slaps in His face.",
"014:066 While Peter was in the courtyard below, one of the servant girls of the high priest came down",
"014:067 and saw him warming himself there. She looked at Peter and said, “You also were with Jesus the Nazarene.”",
"014:068 But he denied it. “I do not know or even understand what you are talking about,” he said. Then he went out to the gateway, and the rooster crowed.",
"014:069 There the servant girl saw him and again said to those standing nearby, “This man is one of them.”",
"014:070 But he denied it again. After a little while, those standing nearby said once more to Peter, “Surely you are one of them, for you too are a Galilean.”",
"014:071 But he began to curse and swear, “I do not know this man of whom you speak!”",
"014:072 And immediately the rooster crowed a second time. Then Peter remembered the word that Jesus had spoken to him: “Before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.” And he broke down and wept."
],
[
"015:001 Early in the morning, the chief priests, elders, scribes, and the whole Sanhedrin devised a plan. They bound Jesus, led Him away, and handed Him over to Pilate.",
"015:002 So Pilate questioned Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?” “You have said so,” Jesus replied.",
"015:003 And the chief priests began to accuse Him of many things.",
"015:004 Then Pilate questioned Him again, “Have You no answer? Look how many charges they are bringing against You!”",
"015:005 But to Pilate’s amazement, Jesus made no further reply.",
"015:006 Now it was Pilate’s custom at the feast to release to the people a prisoner of their choosing.",
"015:007 And a man named Barabbas was imprisoned with the rebels who had committed murder during the insurrection.",
"015:008 So the crowd went up and began asking Pilate to keep his custom.",
"015:009 “Do you want me to release to you the King of the Jews?” Pilate asked.",
"015:010 For he knew it was out of envy that the chief priests had handed Jesus over.",
"015:011 But the chief priests stirred up the crowd to have him release Barabbas to them instead.",
"015:012 So Pilate asked them again, “What then do you want me to do with the One you call the King of the Jews?”",
"015:013 And they shouted back, “Crucify Him!”",
"015:014 “Why?” asked Pilate. “What evil has He done?” But they shouted all the louder, “Crucify Him!”",
"015:015 And wishing to satisfy the crowd, Pilate released Barabbas to them. But he had Jesus flogged, and handed Him over to be crucified.",
"015:016 Then the soldiers led Jesus away into the palace (that is, the Praetorium) and called the whole company together.",
"015:017 They dressed Him in a purple robe, twisted together a crown of thorns, and set it on His head.",
"015:018 And they began to salute Him: “Hail, King of the Jews!”",
"015:019 They kept striking His head with a staff and spitting on Him. And they knelt down and bowed before Him.",
"015:020 After they had mocked Him, they removed the purple robe and put His own clothes back on Him. Then they led Him out to crucify Him.",
"015:021 Now Simon of Cyrene, the father of Alexander and Rufus, was passing by on his way in from the country, and the soldiers forced him to carry the cross of Jesus.",
"015:022 They brought Jesus to a place called Golgotha, which means The Place of the Skull.",
"015:023 There they offered Him wine mixed with myrrh, but He did not take it.",
"015:024 And they crucified Him. They also divided His garments by casting lots to decide what each of them would take.",
"015:025 It was the third hour when they crucified Him.",
"015:026 And the charge inscribed against Him read: THE KING OF THE JEWS.",
"015:027 Along with Jesus, they crucified two robbers, one on His right and one on His left.",
"015:028 OMITTED TEXT",
"015:029 And those who passed by heaped abuse on Him, shaking their heads and saying, “Aha! You who are going to destroy the temple and rebuild it in three days,",
"015:030 come down from the cross and save Yourself!”",
"015:031 In the same way, the chief priests and scribes mocked Him among themselves, saying, “He saved others, but He cannot save Himself!",
"015:032 Let the Christ, the King of Israel, come down now from the cross, so that we may see and believe!” And even those who were crucified with Him berated Him.",
"015:033 From the sixth hour until the ninth hour darkness came over all the land.",
"015:034 At the ninth hour, Jesus cried out in a loud voice, “Eloi, Eloi, lema sabachthani?” which means, “My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?”",
"015:035 When some of those standing nearby heard this, they said, “Behold, He is calling Elijah.”",
"015:036 And someone ran and filled a sponge with sour wine. He put it on a reed and held it up for Jesus to drink, saying, “Leave Him alone. Let us see if Elijah comes to take Him down.”",
"015:037 But Jesus let out a loud cry and breathed His last.",
"015:038 And the veil of the temple was torn in two from top to bottom.",
"015:039 When the centurion standing there in front of Jesus saw how He had breathed His last, he said, “Truly this man was the Son of God!”",
"015:040 And there were also women watching from a distance. Among them were Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James the younger and of Joses, and Salome.",
"015:041 These women had followed Jesus and ministered to Him while He was in Galilee, and there were many other women who had come up to Jerusalem with Him.",
"015:042 Now it was already evening. Since it was Preparation Day (that is, the day before the Sabbath),",
"015:043 Joseph of Arimathea, a prominent Council member who himself was waiting for the kingdom of God, boldly went to Pilate to ask for the body of Jesus.",
"015:044 Pilate was surprised to hear that Jesus was already dead, so he summoned the centurion to ask if this was so.",
"015:045 When Pilate had confirmed it with the centurion, he granted the body to Joseph.",
"015:046 So Joseph bought a linen cloth, took down the body of Jesus, wrapped it in the cloth, and placed it in a tomb that had been cut out of the rock. Then he rolled a stone against the entrance to the tomb.",
"015:047 Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of Joseph saw where His body was placed."
],
[
"016:001 When the Sabbath was over, Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James, and Salome bought spices so they could go and anoint the body of Jesus.",
"016:002 Very early on the first day of the week, just after sunrise, they went to the tomb.",
"016:003 They were asking one another, “Who will roll away the stone from the entrance of the tomb?”",
"016:004 But when they looked up, they saw that the stone had been rolled away, even though it was extremely large.",
"016:005 When they entered the tomb, they saw a young man dressed in a white robe sitting on the right side, and they were alarmed.",
"016:006 But he said to them, “Do not be alarmed. You are looking for Jesus the Nazarene, who was crucified. He has risen! He is not here! See the place where they put Him.",
"016:007 But go, tell His disciples and Peter, ‘He is going ahead of you into Galilee. There you will see Him, just as He told you.’”",
"016:008 So the women left the tomb and ran away, trembling and bewildered. And in their fear they did not say a word to anyone.",
"016:009 Early on the first day of the week, after Jesus had risen, He appeared first to Mary Magdalene, from whom He had driven out seven demons.",
"016:010 She went and told those who had been with Him, who were mourning and weeping.",
"016:011 And when they heard that Jesus was alive and she had seen Him, they did not believe it.",
"016:012 After this, Jesus appeared in a different form to two of them as they walked along in the country.",
"016:013 And they went back and reported it to the rest, but they did not believe them either.",
"016:014 Later, as they were eating, Jesus appeared to the Eleven and rebuked them for their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they did not believe those who had seen Him after He had risen.",
"016:015 And He said to them, “Go into all the world and preach the gospel to every creature.",
"016:016 Whoever believes and is baptized will be saved, but whoever does not believe will be condemned.",
"016:017 And these signs will accompany those who believe: In My name they will drive out demons; they will speak in new tongues;",
"016:018 they will pick up snakes with their hands, and if they drink any deadly poison, it will not harm them; they will lay their hands on the sick, and they will be made well.”",
"016:019 After the Lord Jesus had spoken to them, He was taken up into heaven and sat down at the right hand of God.",
"016:020 And they went out and preached everywhere, and the Lord worked through them, confirming His word by the signs that accompanied it."
]
]
